  "body": "The test binary `wire_post` of `camcraft-app` does not compile on `main` at `83d52ef6a`.\n\n**Cause.** PR #4002 added the field `lead_arc_radius` to `WireContourOp`. The commit `a7a32e421` (#3215) added `crates/app/tests/wire_post/model_arcs.rs` at the same time. That file builds a `WireContourOp` without the new field. Each change was green alone.\n\n**Output.**\n\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `lead_arc_radius` in initializer of `camcraft_app::operation::WireContourOp`\n  --> crates/app/tests/wire_post/model_arcs.rs:42:14\n```\n\n**Command.** `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_post --no-run`\n\n**Fix.** Add `lead_arc_radius: None,` to the `WireContourOp` in `die_of` (`model_arcs.rs`, line 57).\n\nThe branch for #4045 (`mkinney:issue/4045-sodick-ln2w-dialect`) has this one line, because its tests are in the `wire_post` suite. If a different PR fixes this first, that branch takes a merge of `main`.\n\nNo other test file fails for this cause: `wire_dxf_selection` compiles.\n",
